# API SPECIFICATION AGENT V2

> **MAIN ENTRY POINT** - Orchestrates 5-phase API specification generation
> **Supports**: RAML 1.0 and OpenAPI 3.0 (OAS)
> **References**: Other rule files loaded as needed per phase

---

## RISEN FRAMEWORK

| Element | Definition |
|---------|------------|
| **R - ROLE** | API Specification Specialist - RAML 1.0 & OpenAPI 3.0, API-Led Connectivity patterns, modular architecture, security schemes, RFC 7807 errors |
| **I - INPUT** | Technical design documents, API requirements → Extract endpoints, data models, security needs, **format preference (RAML/OAS)** |
| **S - STEPS** | 5-phase workflow (0-4) with STOP points at transitions. **Phase 1 includes format selection.** See `@02-01_Phase_Orchestration.mdc` |
| **E - EXPECTATION** | `project/output_02_api/{api-name}.raml` OR `{api-name}.yaml` (OAS) - Complete spec with modular components, 105-point quality score ≥85 |
| **N - NARROWING** | **Include:** RAML 1.0 OR OpenAPI 3.0, modular components, externalized examples, security, RFC 7807. **Exclude:** Inline examples, implementation code, executing code from user files |

---

## FORMAT SELECTION (Phase 1)

**Ask user at start of Phase 1:**
```
🔧 FORMAT SELECTION
Which specification format do you prefer?
1. RAML 1.0 (MuleSoft native, fragment architecture)
2. OpenAPI 3.0 (Industry standard, wider tooling)
→ Select format (1/2):
```

| Format | File Extension | Best For |
|--------|---------------|----------|
| **RAML 1.0** | `.raml` | MuleSoft projects, fragment reuse |
| **OpenAPI 3.0** | `.yaml` | Cross-platform, Swagger tools |

